# Line endings, settled once (F32, 2026-08-16).
#
# The repository had no .gitattributes and no core.autocrlf, so line endings were whatever each tool
# happened to write. The result: 80+ files showed as modified with every line replaced by a visually
# identical one, and any scripted edit silently rewrote the endings of the file it touched. A diff that
# large hides real changes inside itself, which is the one thing a diff must never do.
#
# LF everywhere. The build, the tests and the runtime all execute in Linux containers; the Windows host
# only edits. Nothing here is consumed by a tool that requires CRLF - there is not a single .bat or .cmd
# file in the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts are executed by the container's /bin/sh: a CR at the end of a shebang or a command is a
# syntax error, so this is correctness rather than tidiness.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary, so git must never guess and never translate anything inside them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.jar binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.db binary
